{"id":"pec_deck","name":"Pec deck","cue":"Keep your elbows soft and squeeze the handles together.","research":"research.json biomech.pec_deck: seated upright against a vertical back pad with the head on the headrest, hips and knees 90, feet flat; elbows soft (20 deg) and fixed; humerus elevation ~80 (elbows just below the shoulders), plane -20 (behind the frontal plane, scapulae retracted 16) -> ~89 (scapulae retracted 5), hands meeting ~45 cm in front of the sternum with the grips ~10 cm apart. Machine: a combination pec fly / rear delt type. The column, overhead frame and bent-tube arms use the same hardware as reverse_fly (tools/design/fly_unit.mjs), but each file sizes its own pad for its seat position (a full back pad here), so the two are not one physical unit. Each handle hinge is the circle through the FK grip at A, mid-rep and B (tools/design/pec_deck.mjs), a near-vertical axis just above the shoulder, so the machine arc is the hand path. The levers hang from bearings on an overhead frame at 0.865 H (the head top is ~0.77 H), carried from the column behind the back pad (the column stops at the beam, no top cap). Each moving arm is one bent tube: a short post out of the bearing, a bend out high above the shoulder, down the outer side of the upper arm and under the forearm into the bottom of the vertical handle, so from the exercise camera it never crosses the chest, the near forearm or the fists (every segment >= 0.02 H off the body). Load: a selectorized weight stack behind the column (two guide rods, cap pulley, cable into the column) rises 0.1 H as the arms close. (tools/design/loads.mjs)","targets":{"tol":10,"tolBy":{"shoulder_plane":12},"note":"shoulder_plane tol 12: with the elbow bent 20 deg and the handles nearly touching ~45-50 cm in front of the sternum (research moving_path), the humerus itself sits at ~89 deg; the research 100 matches the shoulder-to-hand line.","A":{"trunk_flexion":0,"hip_flexion":90,"knee_flexion":90,"shoulder_elevation":80,"shoulder_plane":-20,"elbow_flexion":20},"B":{"trunk_flexion":0,"shoulder_elevation":80,"shoulder_plane":100,"elbow_flexion":20}},"muscles":{"primary":["pec_stern","pec_clav"],"secondary":["delt_ant"],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":25,"el":25,"dAz":0,"dEl":0,"fill":0.58,"note":"Research view az 25 / el 25 (conventions.camera_views), no cheat. A higher, more lateral lens (az 35 / el 33) put the near arm on the view axis at mid-rep, so the near hand seemed to hang beside the seat and the converged fists projected onto the thighs. From az 25 / el 25 both arms sweep visibly around the chest; the fists meet ~47 cm in front of the sternum, 9 cm below shoulder height (FK), which from this lens projects over the upper abdomen, below both pecs, so the chest stays uncovered at the peak."},"rhythm":false,"motion":{"tempo":[1,0.5,2.5,0.5],"root":[0,0.298,0.03],"base":{"pelvis":{"flex":0},"lumbar":{"flex":0},"thorax":{"flex":0},"neck":{"flex":-3},"head":{"flex":0},"thigh_l":{"flex":90,"abd":8},"shank_l":{"flex":90},"foot_l":{"dorsi":0}},"keys":{"A":{"clav_l":{"pro":-16,"elev":-4},"arm_l":{"plane":-4,"elev":85,"rot":0},"fore_l":{"flex":20},"m":{"fly":0}},"B":{"clav_l":{"pro":-5,"elev":-4},"arm_l":{"plane":93.5,"elev":80,"rot":0},"fore_l":{"flex":20},"m":{"fly":-108.09}}}},"pins":[{"landmark":"ischia_c","to":"seat_top"}],"contacts":[{"landmark":"thorax_back","to":"back","tol":0.012},{"landmark":"sacrum","to":"back","tol":0.02},{"landmark":"occiput","to":"headrest","tol":0.012}],"ik":{"hand_l":{"to":"handle_l","pole":"fk","align":"grip_l"}},"machine":{"parts":[{"id":"floor","shape":"box","at":[0,0.0065,0.1],"size":[0.5,0.013,0.64],"mat":"plate","carve":true},{"id":"seatpost","shape":"cyl","from":[0,0.013,0.04],"to":[0,0.212,0.04],"r":0.018,"mat":"frame"},{"id":"seat","shape":"box","at":[0,0.226,0.045],"size":[0.22,0.028,0.25],"mat":"pad","round":0.012},{"id":"seat_top","at":[0,0.24,0]},{"id":"back","shape":"box","at":[0,0.44,-0.059],"size":[0.2,0.32,0.03],"mat":"pad","round":0.012},{"i